IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sgba-nouns`
IMPORT `sgba-seat`

-- Worked cases for sgba-seat.l4 (the neutral part of the seat layer). Each case states facts a person could state and the answer the text of the Act gives, written from the text.
-- Cases about apparatus (a dish, a receiver) are in the quarantined file sgba-tv-cases-seat.l4.

§ `1. Providing a broadcasting service`

-- A person provides a subscription nationwide television service in Singapore, holds no licence, no class licence applies: s 8(1) is contravened.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 6 2025) "subscription nationwide television" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
-- The same person holds a section 8 licence: no.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 6 2025) "subscription nationwide television" FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
-- A class licence applies: no.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 6 2025) "teletext" FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS "No."
-- Not provided in or from Singapore: no.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 6 2025) "subscription nationwide television" FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
-- A service that is or has been an online communication service is not a licensable broadcasting service: no.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 6 2025) "computer online" TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
-- A service not on the Second Schedule is not licensable: no.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 6 2025) "a newsletter by post" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
-- Dates: the first and last day of the deposited text answer; the day before and the day after do not.
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 25 9 2024) "teletext" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 24 9 2024) "teletext" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 1 10 2026) "teletext" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Must I have a licence to provide this service, and am I breaking section 8(1)?` (Date 5 11 2026) "teletext" FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be punished with for providing a licensable broadcasting service without a licence?` EQUALS "A fine of up to $200000, or imprisonment of up to 36 months, or both, and for a continuing offence a further fine of up to $10000 for every day or part of a day it continues after conviction."

-- The Class Licence Notification
#ASSERT `Does the Class Licence Notification make my service subject to the class licence?` (Date 1 6 2025) "audiotext" FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does the Class Licence Notification make my service subject to the class licence?` (Date 1 6 2025) "computer online" FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does the Class Licence Notification make my service subject to the class licence?` (Date 1 6 2025) "computer online" FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Does the Class Licence Notification make my service subject to the class licence?` (Date 1 6 2025) "free-to-air nationwide television" FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Does the Class Licence Notification make my service subject to the class licence?` (Date 21 6 2020) "audiotext" FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."

-- The Exemption Order
#ASSERT `Does the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order exempt me from sections 8 and 9?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order exempt me from sections 8 and 9?` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order exempt me from sections 8 and 9?` (Date 1 6 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Does the Broadcasting (Exemption) Order exempt me from sections 8 and 9?` (Date 14 9 2014) TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not say for that date."

-- Digital display panels
#ASSERT `Does the digital display panels notification make me a class licensee?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 2 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does the digital display panels notification make me a class licensee?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 1 0 FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Does the digital display panels notification make me a class licensee?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 0 3 FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does the digital display panels notification make me a class licensee?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 2 0 FALSE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Does the digital display panels notification make me a class licensee?` (Date 1 6 2025) TRUE 2 0 TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."

§ `2. Decoders and encrypted programmes`

#ASSERT `Is what I do with this decoder prohibited by section 48(1)?` "sell" TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is what I do with this decoder prohibited by section 48(1)?` "let for hire" TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is what I do with this decoder prohibited by section 48(1)?` "sell" TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Is what I do with this decoder prohibited by section 48(1)?` "sell" FALSE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Is what I do with this decoder prohibited by section 48(1)?` "give away for free" TRUE TRUE EQUALS "The Act, as deposited, does not list that act in section 48(1)."
#ASSERT `Does section 48(4) presume that I knew the decoder was unauthorised?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Does section 48(4) presume that I knew the decoder was unauthorised?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Section 48(4) does not presume it on those facts."
#ASSERT `Does section 48(4) presume that I knew the decoder was unauthorised?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS "Section 48(4) does not presume it on those facts."
#ASSERT `Is my reception or rebroadcast of this programme prohibited by section 48(2)?` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is my reception or rebroadcast of this programme prohibited by section 48(2)?` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Is my reception or rebroadcast of this programme prohibited by section 48(2)?` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be punished with for an offence under section 48?` EQUALS "A fine of up to $40000, or imprisonment of up to 36 months, or both."
#ASSERT `May the provider or the copyright owner bring a civil action against me, and is it in time?` TRUE TRUE 10 3 2020 (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS "Yes, and the action is within six years of the act."
#ASSERT `May the provider or the copyright owner bring a civil action against me, and is it in time?` TRUE TRUE 10 3 2020 (Date 11 3 2026) EQUALS "Yes, but section 48A(3) bars an action brought after six years from the act."
#ASSERT `May the provider or the copyright owner bring a civil action against me, and is it in time?` TRUE FALSE 10 3 2020 (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS "No: section 48A(1) needs the act, the decoding and the loss or damage."
#ASSERT `May the provider or the copyright owner bring a civil action against me, and is it in time?` FALSE TRUE 10 3 2020 (Date 10 3 2026) EQUALS "No: section 48A(1) needs the act, the decoding and the loss or damage."

§ `3. If something happens to me`

#ASSERT `Am I, as an officer, guilty as well as the body corporate?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Am I, as an officer, guilty as well as the body corporate?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Am I, as an officer, guilty as well as the body corporate?` FALSE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Can this court try the offence and impose the full penalty?` TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Can this court try the offence and impose the full penalty?` FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I also be prosecuted under the other law, and punished by a higher or other penalty?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `May I also be prosecuted under the other law, and punished by a higher or other penalty?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `May I also be prosecuted under the other law, and punished by a higher or other penalty?` FALSE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Must I provide the document or information the notice asks for?` TRUE TRUE EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Must I provide the document or information the notice asks for?` TRUE FALSE EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be punished with for failing to comply with a section 50 notice or for false information?` EQUALS "A fine of up to $5000, or imprisonment of up to 12 months, or both."
#ASSERT `What is the most I can be fined for obstructing or hindering an employee or agent of the Authority?` EQUALS "A fine of up to $5000, and no imprisonment."

§ `4. When a decision of the Authority goes against me`

#ASSERT `Can I still appeal to the Minister against the Authority's decision under section 12?` 14 EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Can I still appeal to the Minister against the Authority's decision under section 12?` 15 EQUALS "No."
#ASSERT `Is the time the notice gives me for representations long enough under section 10(2)?` 28 EQUALS "Yes."
#ASSERT `Is the time the notice gives me for representations long enough under section 10(2)?` 27 EQUALS "No."
